An invertible 128-dimension flow $f_{\theta}$ maps lattice coefficients to token-logit perturbations while conditioning on a language ID. Training maximises the likelihood of sequences produced by GPT-4o, Llama-3-70B, Mistral-7B, and Phi-3 across thirty-two languages and code-switch corpora. The shared space eliminates per-locale tuning and permits ISA-MAP key rotation without re-training.  
